{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "API, Application Program Interface", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about application program interfaces. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations. Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to communicate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have contact with other applications and transmit information.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's an application program or a function through which you can communicate with libraries or other applications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "engine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the tool or machinery that makes things move.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: An API is an engine that makes possible all the interactivity. In basic words, an API is the messenger that takes requests and tells the system what you want to do and then returns the response back to you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overuse ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "the excessive use of something.", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: But sometimes there are limitations in the APIs so you don't overuse the services but you will have the chance to boost your apps functionality just by adding a couple of codes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the transformation of one message form a language to another", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm reading in the course that an API opens an interface that can connect an app with a particular company's services in order to have all the information that the website provides just by coding the services.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to boost", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to increase, to be better.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(acronym)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: But sometimes there are limitations in the APIs so you don't overuse the services but you will have the chance to boost your apps functionality just by adding a couple of codes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about advantages and common uses of API. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a brochure presenting that information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the brochure with your class and discuss the common uses.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Present and Simple Past of Verb to Be", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the verb <strong><i>be</i></strong> in <strong>present tense</strong> or <strong>past tense</strong> to describe roles, qualities, states or locations.&nbsp;</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>In the <strong>simple present</strong>, you use three irregular forms with the <strong>verb to be</strong> depending on the subject:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i>I <strong>am</strong> aware of the importance of APIs nowadays. </i></li> <li><i>He <strong>is </strong>very talented when dealing with program applications.</i></li> <li><i>They <strong>are</strong> amazed by all the uses APIs have. </i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>In <strong>simple past</strong>, the <strong>verb to be</strong> has two irregular forms. The conjugation changes according to the pronouns too, we use <strong><i>was</i> </strong>with singular pronouns and <strong><i>were</i></strong> with plural pronouns:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i>I <strong>was </strong>aware of the importance of APIs nowadays. </i></li> <li><i>He <strong>was</strong> very talented when dealing with program applications.</i></li> <li><i>They <strong>were</strong> amazed by all the uses APIs have. </i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>To form negative sentences using the <strong>verb to be</strong> in the present or past, you only have to add the word <strong>not</strong> after the verb to be or you can use the contracted forms <strong><i>isn&rsquo;t/aren&rsquo;t</i></strong> or <strong><i>wasn&rsquo;t</i> / <i>weren&rsquo;t</i></strong>.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i>He <strong>isn&rsquo;t </strong>very talented when dealing with program applications.</i></li> <li><i>He <strong>wasn&rsquo;t </strong>very talented when dealing with program applications.</i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>To make questions, the verb <strong>be </strong>and the pronoun switch places:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i><strong>Are</strong> they amazed by all the uses APIs have?</i></li> <li><i><strong>Were</strong> they amazed by all the uses APIs have?</i></li> </ul> <p><i>&nbsp;</i></p> <p>You can also use <i>WH-words</i> when you are asking for specific information:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li><i><strong>What is </strong>the main function of API&rsquo;s?</i></li> <li><i><strong>What was</strong> the main function of API&rsquo;s?</i></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Look at the chart to identify the <strong>verb to </strong>be forms in present and past tenses:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Subject</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Verb Be in Present</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Verb Be in Past</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">I </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> am</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">was</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">You </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> are</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">were</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">He/She/It </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> is</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> was</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">We </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> are</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">were</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">They </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> are</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"> were</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Hey Tim, Can you help me catch up with Mr. Kapoor class? I wasn't there yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is in charge of taking a user request to a specific system and then it takes it back to the user.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Before it was necessary to use high programming level for being able to display text or images on the screen, now it is easier to create software with APIs.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Continuous for Temporary Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the <strong>present continuous tense</strong> to talk about temporary actions that are taking place at the moment or in an unfinished period of time.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>When you make sentences in present continuous, you use the verb to <strong>be</strong> as an auxiliary and you add <strong>&ndash;ING </strong>to the main actions:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>At the moment, <strong><i>I'm programming</i> </strong>an API to link my app with a social network.</li> <li>When you <strong><i>are buying</i></strong> products online, you use API&rsquo;s to look for databases online.</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>To clarify the period of time, you can use time expressions such as <i>now, at the moment, currently, this year, nowadays</i> etc.</p> <p>These are the structures that we can use with the <strong>present continuous</strong>:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Affirmative</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject<strong> + verb Be + main verb in ING + </strong>complement.</p> <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>He <strong>is programming</strong> an API to link his app with a social network.</i></p> <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p><strong>Negative</strong></p> <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject<strong> + verb Be in negative form + main verb in ING + </strong>complement<strong>. </strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>He <strong>isn&rsquo;t programming</strong> an API to link his app with a social network.</i></p> <p><i>&nbsp;</i></p> <p><strong>Interrogative</strong></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Verb Be</strong> + subject + <strong>main verb in ING+</strong> complement?</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><strong><i>Is </i></strong><i>he <strong>programming </strong>an API to link his app with a social network?</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "So, what you are saying is that APIs allows interaction between software applications. Am I right?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In this way, when we are coding APIs, what we are basically doing is requesting other systems to perform a task. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for information about advantages and common uses of API. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a brochure including that information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the brochure with my class discussing the common uses.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to build a brand", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to improve a company's opinion for customers through advertising campaigns.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people use APIs to make money, to sell products online, to save money, to b