"correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "enpe7n2le02ob02re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: Yesterday in my programming class the topic was API. I had problems with it.  <br><span class=\"strong\"> David </span>: That is easy, actually, this is one of the first topics in my programming course. API stands for Application Program Interface. It's an application program or a function through which you can communicate with libraries or other applications. It's a software to obtain information from other applications. For example, look at those apps on your personal email account, they are working very well because the APIs are also functioning correctly.", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "35200", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: All right, but can you explain to me how an API works?  <br><span class=\"strong\"> David </span>: An API is an engine that makes possible all the interactivity. In basic words, an API is a messenger that takes requests and tells the system what you want to do and then returns the response back to you. <br><span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: Was the API concept difficult to develop? <br><span class=\"strong\"> David </span>: Well, it wasn't that much since developers notice all the advantages APIs had like interact with disk files, send data to different parts and bring more functionalities to people. <br><span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: I'm reading in the course that an API opens an interface that can connect an app with a particular company's services in order to have all the information that the website provides just by coding the services.", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "85500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> David </span>: Correct. But sometimes there are limitations in the APIs so you don't overuse the services but you will have the chance to boost your apps functionality just by adding a couple of codes. <br><span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: Are many companies working with API right now? <br><span class=\"strong\"> David </span>: Absolutely. APIs are very useful, you can improve your business with it. Some people use APIs to make money, to sell products online, to save money, to build a brand and many other activities.       <br><span class=\"strong\"> Elizabeth </span>: That information was really important for me. Now I know that an API is a great way to connect different services with each other and bring more functionalities to people.<p>&nbsp;</p>", "image": "enpe7n2le02ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le02ob02re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}